The outcome of the prefetch of an image on the node changed to failed, or from failed.

Published by the image prefetch when the copy and the pull it ran for container resources not started on the node failed, or when the image is in the store of the engine after a prefetch that had failed: pull is the image and where it is fetched to, with its engine, its store, empty for the one of the system, and the identity of its credentials, as the instance configs say it for their resources; state is the outcome, failed, pulled or present; error is what the nodes asked for a copy, then the registry, said of a failed prefetch. The instances whose resources pull the image evaluate their status again, where a missing image whose prefetch failed is a warning. A failed prefetch is tried again later, less and less often, when the configuration of an object pulling the image changes, and when a container of such an object turns up on another node, which then holds the image.
